WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.004
A political crisis and now a

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.705
potential security crisis

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.407
on the streets of Israel

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.375
as the country was brought

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.376
to a standstill

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.844
by the largest general strike

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.579
in Israeli history,

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:13.413
sparked by Prime

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.848
Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.916
plan to weaken the Supreme Court.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:17.884
And his firing

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.386
of the country's defense minister

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.388
for speaking out against the overhaul.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.124
Fiery protests erupted Sunday

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.725
and grew Monday with demonstrators

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.960
descending on Jerusalem

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.229
from all over Israel.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.531
Chanting for democracy

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.198
as they gathered

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.600
in mass in front of the country's

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.768
Supreme Court.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.169
And outside Israel's parliament,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.971
the Knesset nearby.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.706
These changes to the judiciary

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.007
in Israel will be the most significant

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.610
since the country's founding in 1948.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:44.411
Not before

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.345
they will give the Israeli

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.546
parliament, the Knesset

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.914
and therefore whatever parties

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.682
and politicians are in power

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.718
more control over the judiciary

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.453
from how and who the judges are

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.521
who are to be selected

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.856
to even the ability to overturn certain

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.391
Supreme Court decisions.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.460
Now, critics of these reforms fear

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.661
that will destroy the independence

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.196
of the Israeli judiciary.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.197
They would hurt, hurt

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.732
minority rights and would also hurt

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.866
human rights in Israel

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.434
from everything

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.169
from freedom of speech and expression

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.071
to freedom of religion.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.906
On Monday, flights were halted

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.841
and Israel ports stopped work

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.308
alongside

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.543
universities, embassies,

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.946
abroad, malls and even McDonald's slim.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.082
If the leader of Israel's largest

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:22.882
union demanded

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.617
the historic general strike

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.685
to stop what he called

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.053
this judicial revolution,

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.588
this craziness

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.255
it seemed to have

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.924
had the intended effect.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:31.958
Zoom whatever

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:32.859
we are

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:33.893
out of the desire

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.062
to prevent a rift in the nation,

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.697
I decided to suspend the second

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.099
and third reading of the law

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.934
in this session of the Knesset

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.602
to give time to try and reach

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.471
a broad agreement.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.305
For Netanyahu,

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.706
this may be more than just

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.541
a political setback

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.042
Critics say

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.477
the overhaul will help Netanyahu

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.112
in his ongoing corruption trial,

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.880
a charge he denies.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.381
In a Saturday evening interview

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.449
with British journalist Piers

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.184
Morgan, Netanyahu denied

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.520
he was pushing for autocratic rule.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.855
To try to paint me

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.123
as some Third-World

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.891
autocrat is ridiculous.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.359
I believe in the balance.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.695
I'm a classic Democrat with a small view.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.662
I don't want to get into trouble

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.131
with my American friends,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.567
but I am a classic believer

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.468
in the balance

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.303
between the three branches of government.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.339
That's what ensures democracy.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.907
And it's been thrown off

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:21.674
balance in Israel.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.309
We have to bring it back.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.244
Before his speech

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.345
to the nation on Monday,

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.413
he acknowledged the precarious situation

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.515
the country is in

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.415
as some right wing

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.483
groups began calling

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.585
for counter-protests, tweeting.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.953
I call on all the demonstrators

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.321
in Jerusalem on the right

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.290
and the left to behave responsibly

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.558
and not to act violently.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.893
We are brotherly people

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:41.961
with the country in chaos.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:42.929
There are fears now

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.197
that this divisiveness

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:47.567
could still lead to bloodshed.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.803
And while the general strike was lifted

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.138
once the suspension was announced,

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.173
that was also praised

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.474
by the US State Department.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.241
Opposition leaders

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.210
have been a bit more circumspect

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.078
taking more of a wait and see approach,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.480
whether there will actually

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.347
be proper

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.916
negotiations on a compromise

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.717
reform that they want to be mediated

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.386
by the Israeli president Wolf.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.554
All right, Hadas, stay with us.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.288
I also want to bring in

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.456
Israeli journalist Barak Ravid,

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.025
who's covering all of this very closely.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:12.692
Barak.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.259
Prime Minister

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.461
Netanyahu may be backing down for now,

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.030
but without real debate

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.033
could this crisis spiral even further

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.136
I will.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:23.403
Well,

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.604
I think that

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.772
this is definitely

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.674
not the end of this crisis.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.908
I think we're still

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.176
pretty much at the beginning

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.578
because even though Netanyahu

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.813
announced the suspension of the plan

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.448
and the opposition said

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.350
that it's ready for a dialog.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.452
The gaps are pretty big.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.254
And I think that

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.890
it is not an unlikely scenario

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.092
that several weeks will pass.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.160
It will have several rounds

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.661
of negotiation,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.762
reach a deadlock,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.964
and then we will see

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:53.099
a rerun of everything

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:55.802
we've seen in the last few weeks.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.570
As you know, Israelis have been out there

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.305
protesting on the streets of Israel

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.340
for months now.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.442
How did it get to this point, Barak?

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.644
How concerned are Israelis

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.879
about an authoritarian lurch

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.748
that potentially is out there

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.019
I think that obviously

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.921
on Sunday night

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:18.091
when when Netanyahu decided to fire

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.693
the minister of defense, you have Garland

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.463
just because he did his job and warned

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.299
that this judicial overhaul is a clear

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.533
and immediate threat to Israel

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.835
national security.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.671
I think this is when the penny drop,

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:34.741
not only for the usual suspects, people

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.676
that did not vote for Netanyahu.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.511
I think the penny then dropped

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.648
for a lot of Likud vote And I think that

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:44.284
then you saw a spontaneous

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:48.288
rage erupt around the country,

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:49.956
which led to again,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.225
hundreds of thousands of people

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.126
in the streets.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.095
And I think that in a way, we know today

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.597
that three months

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.732
after this whole thing started,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.901
for Netanyahu politically,

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.169
this was like hitting

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.071
the self-destruct button.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.906
You saw the polls tonight

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.541
in three different Israeli

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.909
television channels.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.813
All of them showed that Netanyahu is at

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.281
above.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:18.217
65% unfavorability.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.920
He never had those lowest numbers.

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.288
Hadas,

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.290
some are vowing to continue protesting

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.858
on the streets of Israel.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.194
Where do you think things go from here?

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.264
Well, I definitely think the protests

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:31.931
will continue

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.099
because the protesters

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.634
now, we've seen them both

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.768
for this reform

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:36.569
coming out tonight,

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.603
as well as the protesters

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.439
who have been out for 12 weeks now

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:40.340
against reform.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.407
They have a lot of energy.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.009
They have a lot of organization

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:43.743
behind them.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.510
And a lot of them,

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.045
I think, do not believe

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.513
Netanyahu at his word

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.114
when he says he's

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.549
going to suspend the legislation.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.117
They're going to also want to see

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:51.584
whether there

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.186
will be real negotiations

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.922
over a possible compromise. 

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.090
Hadas Gold and Barak Ravid, guys,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.391
thank you very, very much.

